{"step_index":2281,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T15:26:11Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T15:26:11Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T15:26:11Z\nShowing lines 270-340 of 492\n270: /// Dispatch over the bridge's shared lungs socket. The connection first binds\n271: /// to this identity's session, so no credential crosses it. An empty session\n272: /// calls the no-argument container bootstrap; the bridge derives identity\n273: /// from its kernel peer and native Incus binding. A named session uses the\n274: /// host-root-only bootstrap. Both run through the identity's own grants.\n275: pub async fn call_over_socket(\n276:     socket: &Path,\n277:     session: &str,\n278:     plugin_id: &str,\n279:     method_name: &str,\n280:     method: &MethodDecl,\n281:     arguments: Value,\n282: ) -> Result<CallReceipt, LungsError> {\n283:     validate_arguments(method, &arguments)?;\n284:     let operation_id = uuid::Uuid::new_v4().to_string();\n285:     let stream = tokio::time::timeout(\n286:         LUNGS_NEGOTIATION_TIMEOUT,\n287:         tokio::net::UnixStream::connect(socket),\n288:     )\n289:     .await\n290:     .map_err(|_| LungsError::Transport(\"lungs socket connection timed out\".into()))?\n291:     .map_err(|error| LungsError::Transport(format!(\"connect to {}: {error}\", socket.display())))?;\n292:     let connection = tokio::time::timeout(\n293:         LUNGS_NEGOTIATION_TIMEOUT,\n294:         zbus::connection::Builder::unix_stream(stream)\n295:             .p2p()\n296:             .auth_mechanism(zbus::connection::AuthMechanism::Anonymous)\n297:             .build(),\n298:     )\n299:     .await\n300:     .map_err(|_| LungsError::Transport(\"lungs socket negotiation timed out\".into()))?\n301:     .map_err(|error| LungsError::Transport(format!(\"lungs socket: {error}\")))?;\n302:     let lungs = tokio::time::timeout(\n303:         LUNGS_NEGOTIATION_TIMEOUT,\n304:         Proxy::new(\n305:             &connection,\n306:             PLUGIN_BUS_NAME,\n307:             LUNGS_OBJECT_PATH,\n308:             LUNGS_INTERFACE,\n309:         ),\n310:     )\n311:     .await\n312:     .map_err(|_| LungsError::Transport(\"lungs bind proxy timed out\".into()))?\n313:     .map_err(|error| LungsError::Transport(format!(\"lungs bind proxy: {error}\")))?;\n314:     let binding = tokio::time::timeout(LUNGS_NEGOTIATION_TIMEOUT, async {\n315:         if session.is_empty() {\n316:             lungs.call(\"BindCurrentContainer\", &()).await\n317:         } else {\n318:             lungs.call(\"Bind\", &(session,)).await\n319:         }\n320:     })\n321:     .await\n322:     .map_err(|_| LungsError::Transport(\"lungs identity bind timed out\".into()))?;\n323:     let bound: bool = binding.map_err(|error| match refusal(&error) {\n324:         true => LungsError::Registration(error.to_string()),\n325:         false => LungsError::Transport(format!(\"bind: {error}\")),\n326:     })?;\n327:     if !bound {\n328:         return Err(LungsError::Registration(\n329:             \"bridge declined to bind this session\".into(),\n330:         ));\n331:     }\n332:     let result = plugin_call(\n333:         &connection,\n334:         plugin_id,\n335:         method_name,\n336:         &arguments,\n337:         &operation_id,\n338:     )\n339:     .await?;\n340:     receipt(plugin_id, method_name, method, result, &operation_id)"}
{"step_index":2282,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T15:26:11Z","input_tokens":3580,"cache_read_tokens":147103,"output_tokens":1669,"content":"On the **FUSE side**, the entry point for an external node operates through **`3tched-fs`'s dual-lungs dispatch**:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Can an External Node Mount FUSE Directly?\n**Yes.** `3tched-fs` was explicitly designed so it doesn't have to live solely inside the local container.\n\nLook at `crates/threetched-fs/src/main.rs:250`:\n```rust\n/// The identity's SID1 on its own device, registered per call.\n#[arg(long)]\nlungs_credential: Option<PathBuf>,\n#[arg(long, default_value = DEFAULT_BUS_ADDRESS)]\nbus_address: String,\n```\n\nIf an external node (e.g. an edge worker or a remote subsidiary) has an authored **cryptographic ID card (its `SID1` credential)**:\n* It runs `3tched-fs` on its **own machine**.\n* It passes `--lungs-credential /path/to/identity.sid1` and `--bus-address <bridge_door_address>`.\n* **FUSE mounts the typed filesystem locally on that external node**.\n* The external node now does `cat` and `write` to local inodes, and `3tched-fs` transparently bridges every file operation over the wire with the caller's SID1 attached to each call!\n\n---\n\n### 2. Inside the Local Container: Where Do External Invocations Show Up?\n\nInside the container's own FUSE mount (`/run/opdbus/lungs/`), how does it perceive external nodes knocking on the door?\n\nEvery plugin in the sealed catalog projects three virtual inodes on the FUSE side:\n```\n/run/opdbus/lungs/plugins/<plugin_id>/operations/<method>/\n├── input     <-- Typed schema describing the arguments\n├── output    <-- Result receipt from the last invocation\n└── call      <-- The execution entry point (CallFile)\n```\n\n1. **The `CallFile` Inode**:\n   * As defined in `crates/threetched-fs/src/namespace.rs:96`:\n     > *\"A complete JSON write, flushed on close, is validated against the sealed method schema and dispatched as the mount's identity.\"*\n   * Writing JSON to `.../call` and closing the file descriptor is the **atomic entry point** for invoking any method on the FUSE side.\n2. **The Inbound Arrival (Chat Response & Events)**:\n   * When an external node sends a request through Door `:8090`, it writes to the `chat_response` queue.\n   * On the container's FUSE side, the identity sees the arrival at:\n     `/run/opdbus/lungs/plugins/chat_response/`\n   * The container reads the incoming turn, processes it through its cognitive memory loop, and writes its response to:\n     `/run/opdbus/lungs/plugins/chat_response/operations/submit_turn/call`.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of the FUSE Entry Point\n\n* **For the Local Container**: The entry point is writing to **`.../operations/<method>/call`** inside `/run/opdbus/lungs/`.\n* **For an External Node**: The entry point is running **`3tched-fs --lungs-credential <sid1>`**, which projects that same typed VFS tree on the external node over the network.","thinking":"The code segment describes how a bridge handles connections. It establishes that a session binding occurs initially, preventing credential leakage. An empty session triggers a container bootstrap with identity derived from the kernel peer and binding, while a named session uses a host-root-only bootstrap. Both bootstraps leverage the session's specific grants.\n\n\nAn external node can mount the FUSE file system by running the `3tched-fs` process locally, using its own SID1 credential. This is achieved by specifying the credential path and the bus address for the bridge. This implies a local FUSE mount on the external machine. It then connects to the bridge using its unique credentials, as the bridge acts as the entry point.\n\n\n"}
