{"step_index":2285,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T15:26:33Z","input_tokens":2300,"cache_read_tokens":150761,"output_tokens":1503,"content":"You are completely right about the vertical orientation:\n\n**Blobs down at the bottom (the bedrock). Node up at the top (the FUSE side).**\n\nThe sealed blobs are the foundational roots; the FUSE filesystem is the living canopy at the top where the node actually lives and breathes.\n\n---\n\n### The True Vertical Stack (Bedrock to Canopy)\n\n```\n       ▲  [ TOP: THE NODE (FUSE SIDE) ]\n       │  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n       │  • The Node lives here: files, directories, inodes.\n       │  • Local POSIX operations: `cat /call`, `ls /plugins`.\n       │  • Whether the node is local or external, it interacts HERE.\n       │\n       │  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n       │  [ MIDDLE: THE CONDUIT & SPINAL CORD ]\n       │  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n       │  • Tonic gRPC Door / Unix Domain Socket / D-Bus Bus.\n       │  • Carries the signals between the bedrock and the node.\n       │  • No business logic; pure transport and admission enforcement.\n       │\n       ▼  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n          [ BOTTOM: THE SEALED BLOBS & SHM ]\n          ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n          • The immutable bedrock: `opblob` + SHM state buffers.\n          • Contains the absolute truth: schemas, hashes, capabilities.\n          • Anchors everything; cannot be mutated from above.\n```\n\n---\n\n### How the External Node Operates in This Vertical Stack\n\n1. **The Bedrock Down at the Bottom (`Blobs`)**:\n   * Anchors the entire universe. It defines what capabilities exist, what arguments are valid, and who has permission.\n   * Startup only consumes sealed blobs—it never writes to them.\n\n2. **The Canopy Up at the Top (`Node / FUSE side`)**:\n   * The node sits at the top on the **FUSE side**.\n   * It doesn't see raw binary blobs, database transactions, or socket protocols. It sees a clean, typed filesystem.\n   * When the node wants to act, it writes JSON into a `.../call` file at the top.\n\n3. **The Vertical Gravity**:\n   * The file write at the top falls down through the conduit.\n   * It hits the bedrock (the sealed blob) to verify the schema hash and capability.\n   * If the bedrock approves, the action executes, and the receipt bubbles back up to the top as a virtual `output` file.\n\nThe **Blobs are the earth below**; the **FUSE Node is the living entity above**.","thinking":"Hypothesis: user is conceptually modeling data distribution across nodes. Initial interpretation: \"blobs\" reside at a bottom node, another node is at the top, and \"fuseside\" represents a merging point. Further clarification needed to understand the overall architecture they're envisioning, to see if it is consistent with system's behavior. The phrasing suggests a possible misconception about data locality or node roles.\n\n\nThe user's model clarifies the hierarchy: the FUSE-facing node is at the top, projecting upwards from the \"blobs\" at the bottom. These \"blobs\" represent the foundational, immutable state. Data flow appears to go from the bottom blobs, through a translation layer, to the top node, which presents the FUSE interface.\n\n\n"}
