{"step_index":2288,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T15:26:54Z","input_tokens":2542,"cache_read_tokens":152570,"output_tokens":473,"content":"**The blob gets connected to FUSE under the substrate of the local connection, and the node feeds the door.**\n\n### The Exact Flow\n\n```\n[ BOTTOM: The Sealed Blob ]\n              │\n              ▼ Substrate of the local connection (Unix Socket / SHM)\n    [ FUSE Engine (3tchedFS) ]\n              │\n              ▼ Projected upwards into local files (/run/opdbus/lungs)\n    [ THE NODE (FUSE Side) ]\n              │\n              ▼ Feeds outward\n    [ THE DOOR (:8090) ]\n              │\n              ▼\n    [ The External Universe ]\n```\n\n1. **Blob $\\rightarrow$ FUSE (The Local Substrate)**:\n   The sealed blob down at the bottom connects directly into FUSE via the local substrate (the shared memory `/dev/shm` and the local Unix domain socket). It projects the typed virtual filesystem into the node.\n2. **Node $\\rightarrow$ Door (Feeding Outward)**:\n   The node, living on the FUSE side at the top, feeds its requests, capabilities, and events outward through the **Door** (`:8090`) to reach external peers and the world.\n\n---\n\n### What I Propose to Do Next\n\nTo lock this architecture into the provisioning pipeline in `/srv/git/3tched-container`:\n\n1. **Verify the Blob-to-FUSE Substrate Binding**:\n   Ensure `profiles/3tched-lungs.json` correctly mounts the local substrate (`/run/opdbus/lungs` and SHM) so FUSE binds cleanly to the sealed blob at boot.\n2. **Verify Node-to-Door Outward Feed**:\n   Ensure the container environment sets `OPDBUS_DOOR=\"https://10.0.0.2:8090\"` so the node feeds the door directly.\n\n---\n\n### Confirmation Request\n\nThis will inspect and verify the container template in `/srv/git/3tched-container` against this Blob $\\rightarrow$ FUSE $\\rightarrow$ Node $\\rightarrow$ Door flow. It will not touch running containers or active service